  "title": "Face processing MEEG dataset with HED annotation",
  "description": "This dataset contains the simultaneous MEG and EEG recordings, together with structural MRI, from the multi-subject, multi-modal face processing dataset originally released by Wakeman and Henson (ds000117). Eighteen participants viewed famous, unfamiliar, and scrambled faces and made a symmetry judgment with a key press. The events have been augmented and reorganized, annotated with Hierarchical Event Descriptors (HED), and the EEG repackaged in BioSemi Data Format.",
  "methods_description": "Eighteen participants completed two sessions three months apart, one with fMRI and one with simultaneous MEG and EEG. In each session they judged the relative spatial symmetry of famous, unfamiliar, and scrambled face photographs, and each face was presented twice, either immediately or after a delay of 5-15 presentations. The EEG was extracted from the MEG/EEG fif files, fiducials were added, channels renamed, events extracted and corrected for a 34 ms latency shift, button presses added, and HED annotations applied. The recordings were then converted to BDF with biosigio.",
